## Test 6: Workflows Can Be Invoked via Sub-Agents ✅

### Invocation Chain

```
User / Main Agent
  → delegate("dev-mas-engineer")
    → delegate("sub_mas-dev-director")
      → delegate("sub_mas-workflow-engine", "workflow: wf_recovery_*")
        → workflow engine reads SOT workflows.yaml
        → executes steps (shell, delegate, parallel, conditional, loop, etc.)
        → returns structured mas_result YAML
```

### Recovery Workflow Invocability

| # | Workflow | Sub-Agent | CLI Trigger | SOT ID |
|---|----------|-----------|-------------|--------|
| 1 | Immune | `sub_mas-recovery-immune` | `recovery --immune` | `wf_recovery_immune` |
| 2 | Checkpoint | `sub_mas-recovery-checkpoint` | `recovery --checkpoint` | `wf_recovery_checkpoint` |
| 3 | Safezone | `sub_mas-recovery-safezone` | `recovery --safezone` | `wf_recovery_safezone` |
| 4 | Timeline | `sub_mas-recovery-timeline` | `recovery --timeline` | `wf_recovery_timeline` |
| 5 | Defib | `sub_mas-recovery-defib` | `recovery --defib` | `wf_recovery_defib` |

### Workflow Engine Capabilities

The `sub_mas-workflow-engine` supports **10 action types**:
`shell` · `delegate` · `write` · `read` · `signal` · `rule_check` · `parallel` · `conditional` · `loop` · `wait_for_user` · `calculate`

Workflows are **SOT-driven** — loaded from `.state/workflows.yaml`, not hardcoded.

### Agent Task-to-Workflow Mappings

| Agent | Tasks Mapped |
|-------|-------------|
| recovery-immune | `CHECK_YAML` → `wf_immune_check_yaml`, `CHECK_SYNTAX` → `wf_immune_check_syntax`, `VERIFY_STATE` → `wf_immune_verify_state` |
| recovery-checkpoint | `SNAPSHOT` → `wf_checkpoint_snapshot`, `LIST` → `wf_checkpoint_list`, `RESTORE` → `wf_checkpoint_restore`, `DIFF` → `wf_checkpoint_diff` |
| recovery-safezone | `FORK` → `wf_safezone_fork`, `MERGE` → `wf_safezone_merge`, `ABORT` → `wf_safezone_abort`, `DIFF` → `wf_safezone_diff` |
| recovery-timeline | `FIND_BEST` → `wf_timeline_findbest`, `RESTORE_BEST` → `wf_timeline_restore`, `SHOW_PATH` → `wf_timeline_showpath`, `ANALYZE` → `wf_timeline_analyze` |
| recovery-defib | `DEFIB` → `wf_defib_execute`, `RESURRECT` → `wf_defib_resurrect`, `DIAGNOSE` → `wf_defib_diagnose` |

